-- PREMIUM / HARD — Stimulus: Recycling
(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',3,'READING','Comprehension – Literal',5,
'Recycling plays a vital role in protecting Australia''s environment. When we recycle materials such as paper, glass, plastic and aluminium, we reduce the amount of rubbish sent to landfill. Producing goods from recycled materials requires significantly less energy than manufacturing from raw resources. Recycling aluminium, for example, uses approximately 95% less energy than producing it from bauxite ore. However, recycling only works when correct items are placed in recycling bins. Contaminated loads — those containing wrong items or food waste — are often rejected at sorting facilities and sent directly to landfill. Schools across Australia are teaching students the importance of correct sorting to maximise recycling rates.','TEXT',
'PREMIUM','HARD',
'What happens to contaminated loads of recycling?','{"A":"They are carefully sorted","B":"They are cleaned and reused","C":"They are sent to landfill","D":"They are composted"}','{"value":"C"}','The passage states contaminated loads are rejected and sent directly to landfill.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
